terryk1463@yahoo.com (I Must Be Crazy 2) writes:
> If a chameleon/doppelganger were to mimic a dragon (not by using a
> potion/wand of polymorph) and I kill it in that form, would I get the
> big Experience points as if I actually killed a dragon?

Up to a point. Though shapeshifters revert to their natural form on
death, they keep the same number of hit dice; thus, the parts of the
XP formula that derives from monster level will depend on what form it
was in when it died. However, eligibility for the various bonuses (AC,
speed, special attacks, and nastiness) will derive from its own form
(which generally rules out most of them).

